  "body": "## What changed\n\nA stock-source Face got a false `Gouge` on its last row when that row was tangent to the stock edge. The row was above the stock top and the document had no part. The post refused the program (#1659).\n\n**Root cause.** The stock outline has vertices on its straight sides: `(62, 60)`, `(-2, 60)`, `(0, 62)` and `(0, -2)`. The last row (`(-4, 60) -> (64, 60)`) goes exactly through `(-2, 60)` and `(62, 60)`. The Boundary wall reading of law (b) with no model (`wall_gouge` in `crates/sim/src/verify/section.rs`) excuses a row that crosses the rim. But it counted only a proper crossing through the interior of an edge. A row through a vertex crossed no edge interior. Thus the law read it as a move in the region, at distance 0 from the vertex, and gave `Gouge { at: 42 }`. The first row (y 0) got no warning because no vertex is on its line. The cause was not the keep law of #1607, the stock sim or a tolerance sign.\n\n**Fix.** A new helper `crosses_rim` (`section.rs`) also counts a pass through a loop vertex when the two neighbours of the vertex are on opposite sides of the trace (`Trace::through` in `crates/sim/src/verify/arc_wall.rs`, for a segment, an XY arc and an XZ / YZ footprint, within `CROSSING_TOUCH`). A touch at a vertex (both neighbours on one side) is not a crossing and stays a gouge. No tolerance changed; `GOUGE_TOL` stays 0.01.\n\n## How tested\n\nPins, each mutation-checked:\n\n| Pin | Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| app `face_stock_edge::a_face_row_tangent_to_the_stock_edge_in_air_with_no_part_is_clean_and_posts` (the issue's exact repro, move 42, posts) | M1: no vertex crossing (the old law) | fails |\n| sim `boundary_walls::a_row_through_two_side_vertices_tangent_to_the_far_edge_crosses_the_rim_and_is_clean` | M1 | fails |\n| sim `boundary_walls::a_move_inside_or_only_touching_a_vertex_still_answers_to_the_walls` | M2: every vertex a crossing | fails (and the #43 corner pin fails too) |\n| app `face_stock_edge::the_same_face_over_a_part_whose_top_stands_above_cut_z_is_refused` | M5: keep law gets no parts | fails |\n| app `face_stock_edge::a_tangent_last_row_0_02_mm_into_a_part_is_refused` (only the last row is convicted; the post stops) | M3: `GOUGE_TOL` 0.03; M5 | fails |\n\nWith the fix, all pins pass. Note: M4 (laws b and b2 off in the sim verifier) does not break the two part pins. The keep law in the operation layer convicts them.\n\nGates:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (sim lib, `boundary_arc_planes`, `boundary_arc_walls`, `boundary_walls`, `model_excess`; app `coarse_rims`, `face_stock_edge`, `real_tip_contour`, `slot_caps`, `thread_mill_rim`, `verify_arc_reading`).\n- Also run: app `area_controls`, `area_open`, `stock_source_law`, `after_op`, `accessory_collisions`, `post_not_judged`: green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets --no-deps -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- The batch and release tiers, and the GUI.\n- The arc branch of `Trace::through` has no direct pin. A Face row is a straight move.\n- I did not find why the stock outline carries vertices on its sides. A vertex on a straight side is a correct loop, so the verifier now reads it correctly (see the decision file).\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/1659-face-rim-vertex-crossing.md`.\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0; branch made from `upstream/main` (2b6e03f).\n\nChangelog: A Face on the stock whose last row is tangent to the stock edge, with no part, no longer gets a false Gouge and posts (#1659).\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1659\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
